# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts to CRLF on checkout by default, which is fine for
# Kotlin and XML and fatal for anything with a shebang: a shell script with
# CRLF endings has an interpreter line of "#!/bin/sh\r", the kernel cannot
# resolve it, and the error is "not found" for a file that is plainly there.
#
# That bit the hub's first container build — `gradlew` had been copied from a
# Windows working tree, and the Docker build failed at step 7 with exit 127.
# The Dockerfile now strips CR defensively as well; this stops the file from
# acquiring them in the first place.

*           text=auto
gradlew     text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Windows-only, and cmd.exe genuinely wants CRLF.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.apk       binary
*.keystore  binary
*.jar       binary
